pathwidth itself: each equals\npathwidth or pathwidth plus one. Two lie in bands one and two wide, and two are\nfalse as stated; every relation is proved, and machine-checked in Lean.\nSecond, the literature has settled on the name pathwidth, used more than three\ntimes as often as the other eleven names together, and the three communities\nrarely cite one another. Third, the best exact algorithm for MOSP, the search of\n\\citet{ChuStuckey2009}, is a pathwidth algorithm, and two of its published\ndominance theorems are false. The correct rule was already known for\npathwidth; we show that it is tested by one bipartite matching per candidate,\nand prove the repaired search sound. In our implementation it costs at most\n2\\% more search nodes on each benchmark set, and it re-proved all 115 benchmark\noptima that rested on the published rules, changing none. Fourth, we release\n17,714 benchmark graphs, distinct up to isomorphism, from twenty collections,\n16,087 of them with a certified pathwidth and a layout that attains it.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\input{sec1_intro}\n\\input{sec2_equivalences}\n\\input{sec3_names}\n\\input{sec4_search}\n\\input{sec5_results}\n\\input{sec6_conclusion}\n\\input{sec7_data}\n\n\\bibliography{refs}\n\n\\appendix\n\\input{sec9a_appendix_lean}\n\\input{sec9b_appendix_machinery}\n\\input{sec9c_appendix_names}\n\n\\end{document}\n# Builds paper2/latex/main.pdf, the first full draft of paper 2.\n#   make          latexmk -pdf (pdflatex + bibtex as often as needed)\n#   make tables   regenerate tables/*.tex from the recorded CSVs\n#   make refs     check every DOI in refs.bib against Crossref / DataCite (cached)\n#   make axioms   every theorem the draft cites has a clean axiom line (needs lake build)\n#   make check    fail on undefined references or citations in the last build\n#   make clean    remove build products but the PDF\nall: main.pdf\n\nmain.pdf: main.tex $(wildcard sec*.tex) refs.bib $(wildcard tables/*.tex) $(wildcard ../figures/*.pdf)\n\tlatexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error main.tex\n\ntables:\n\tcd ../.. && python3 -m paper2.latex.make_tables\n\nrefs:\n\tcd ../.. && python3 -m paper2.latex.check_refs\n\naxioms:\n\tcd ../.. && python3 -m paper2.latex.check_axioms\n\ncheck: main.pdf\n\t@! grep -E \"undefined|Citation .* undefined|Reference .* undefined\" main.log\n\t@echo \"no undefined references; $$(pdfinfo main.pdf | grep Pages)\"\n\nclean:\n\tlatexmk -c\n\trm -f *.bbl *.blg *.synctex.gz\n\ndistclean: clean\n\trm -f main.pdf\n\n.PHONY: all tables refs axioms check clean distclean\ntests/test_paper2_latex.py\n12:def test_every_cited_lean_name_is_declared():\n17:def test_every_doi_is_in_the_checked_cache():\n26:def test_every_citation_key_is_in_the_bibliography():\n35:def test_cost_table_reproduces_the_recorded_ratios():\n42:def test_certificates_table_reproduces_the_recorded_totals():\n48:def test_every_cited_theorem_has_an_axiom_line():","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1c55f7b-98f8-4ea9-815f-35ebfa760af6","uuid":"82e49012-3d4c-4e90-934d-85ec13e41095","timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:44:16.601Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\theoremstyle{definition}\n\\newtheorem{definition}[theorem]{Definition}\n\\newtheorem{counterexample}[theorem]{Counterexample}\n\\theoremstyle{remark}\n\\newtheorem*{remark}{Remark}\n\n\\newcommand{\\pw}{\\mathrm{pw}}\n\\newcommand{\\vs}{\\mathrm{vs}}\n\\newcommand{\\ns}{\\mathrm{ns}}\n\\newcommand{\\mns}{\\mathrm{mns}}\n\\newcommand{\\es}{\\mathrm{es}}\n\\newcommand{\\pes}{\\mathrm{pes}}\n\\newcommand{\\sbw}{\\mathrm{sb}}\n\\newcommand{\\cw}{\\mathrm{cw}}\n\\newcommand{\\mcw}{\\mathrm{mcw}}\n\\newcommand{\\cl}{\\mathrm{cl}}\n\\newcommand{\\Sol}{\\mathrm{Sol}}\n\\newcommand{\\cost}{\\mathrm{cost}}\n\\newcommand{\\open}{\\mathrm{open}}\n\\newcommand{\\close}{\\mathrm{close}}\n\\newcommand{\\fin}{\\mathrm{fin}}\n\\newcommand{\\pla}{\\mathrm{pla}}\n\\newcommand{\\VSG}{\\mathrm{VSG}}\n\\newcommand{\\placeholder}[1]{\\par\\noindent\\fbox